# mpd.env — settings for this Moodle project.
#
# Edit this file to change how this one project runs: which database it
# uses, which PHP version, whether Behat is set up. Every setting is
# optional. Leave a line out and mpd uses a default.
#
# Two ways to change a setting:
#
#   mpd start <project> MPD_DB=postgres:18
#       Checks the value, writes the line, and applies the change.
#
#   Edit this file by hand, then run: mpd start <project>
#       Accepts any value. The second command is what applies it.
#
# To switch off something that is on by default, give it an empty value.
# MPD_DB="" means this project gets no database.
#
# mpd wrote this file when you ran `mpd init` and will never overwrite
# it. Git ignores it.
#
# Where defaults come from and which file wins when two disagree:
# docs/architecture.md, section 8.


# Database
#
# Which database engine and version to run, written like a container tag.
#
#   Engines:   postgres, mariadb, mysql
#   Versions:  a number (18, 17.2, 17-bookworm) or the word latest
#   Engine alone (postgres) means the latest version of it.
#
# Moodle needs a database. Leave this out and mpd uses the Moodle default
# from
# /opt/mpd/assets/vm/project_types/moodle/mpd-defaults.env (postgres:17,
# matching the mdl-demo demo). Set MPD_DB="" only to give this project no
# database, which stops mpd writing config.php.
#MPD_DB=postgres:17


# PHP version
#
# One of: 8.1, 8.2, 8.3, 8.4, 8.5.
# Leave this out to use the Moodle default (8.3, matching the mdl-demo
# demo) from
# /opt/mpd/assets/vm/project_types/moodle/mpd-defaults.env.
#
# You can change it at any time. `mpd start <project>` switches a
# running project over.
#MPD_PHP_VERSION=8.4


# Behat
#
# Behat is on: mpd publishes https://behat.<project>.<zone>/ and adds that
# name to the certificate. Set this to 0 to switch it off for this project.
#
# Tests run in headless Chromium. To watch one in a browser window on the
# desktop, run: behat --profile=headed <feature>
#MPD_MOODLE_BEHAT=0

# External test files for phpunit
#
# Some phpunit tests download files, such as test.html and test_redir.php,
# from a web server. mpd serves them from the exttests project on this VM.
#
# To test against an older version of the files, clone that branch of
# https://github.com/moodlehq/moodle-exttests.git into a new project, for
# example /srv/projects/exttests405. Then run:
#
#   mpd init exttests405
#   mpd start exttests405
#   mpd start <this project> MPD_MOODLE_EXTTESTS=exttests405
#
# To skip these tests, write MPD_MOODLE_EXTTESTS="" in this file, then run
# mpd start <this project>. Some of them then fail with "The data provider
# ... is invalid".
#MPD_MOODLE_EXTTESTS=exttests405


# Extra services
#
# Comma-separated shared service containers this project needs. mpd starts
# them on `mpd start` — the way it ensures your database — and wires them into
# the config:
#
#   mailpit     Catch-all mail. Moodle sends into it and you read the messages
#               in its web UI, so no real mail ever leaves. List it here and
#               Moodle is pointed at it; leave it out and Moodle is set to
#               noemailever and sends nothing.
#   adminer     Database admin web UI.
#
# Off by default: a project that lists nothing gets noemailever and no extra
# containers. A service you want up on its own, without a project asking for
# it, is `mpd --service-start <name>` instead.
#MPD_REQUIRE_SERVICES=mailpit
